{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39835986",
      "title": "Styling React Apps with Inline Styles",
      "sourceHash": "10b52e59fb0ade036d9f2bfba7b545b4f004721a8b28c465bb0c7c23bade141b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 1.74,
          "en": "So we got this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.74,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "at least potential disadvantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "that CSS code is not scoped to components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 11.52,
          "en": "when using vanilla CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.52,
          "end": 13.23,
          "en": "So what can we do about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.23,
          "end": 16.08,
          "en": "if we wanna achieve some scoping?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.08,
          "end": 21.08,
          "en": "Well, one solution would be to switch to inline styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.78,
          "end": 26.78,
          "en": "So to apply these paragraph styles inline to the paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.94,
          "end": 29.493,
          "en": "to which they should apply, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.33,
          "end": 32.94,
          "en": "And inline styles simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 37.5,
          "en": "that instead of defining CSS styles in a CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.5,
          "end": 40.053,
          "en": "you apply them right in your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.92,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "And you can do that in React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 46.68,
          "en": "by setting the style prop on JSX elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.68,
          "end": 50.793,
          "en": "just as you can set the style attribute in vanilla HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 55.95,
          "en": "The style prop does not take a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 59.46,
          "en": "which then contains color red, for example, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "even though that is how you would use this attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "in just HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 67.7,
          "en": "But if you would try to use that here in JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.7,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "in your React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 70.93,
          "en": "you'll see that you get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.06,
          "end": 75.42,
          "en": "that the style prop expects a mapping",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.42,
          "end": 79.473,
          "en": "of style properties to values, not a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.43,
          "end": 83.01,
          "en": "So this is not how you should use the style prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.01,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "in JSX in React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "Instead the style prop takes a dynamic value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "hence we need the opening and closing curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 97.68299999999999,
          "en": "and then you pass an object as a value to the style prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.64,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "And that's important to understand here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 106.1,
          "en": "This here is not some special double curly brace syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 109.25999999999999,
          "en": "you have to use for styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "instead this is the regular dynamic value syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 116.85,
          "en": "where you then just pass an object as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.85,
          "end": 119.913,
          "en": "instead of a number, or a boolean, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.65,
          "end": 123.39,
          "en": "And it's now in this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.39,
          "end": 125.34,
          "en": "where you set up the styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.34,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "that should be applied to this paragraph as key-value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 131.16,
          "en": "So that for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.16,
          "end": 135.39,
          "en": "if you would want to give this paragraph a red color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.39,
          "end": 137.883,
          "en": "you would add color as a key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.9,
          "end": 143.55,
          "en": "and then a colon, since we are in a JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.55,
          "end": 146.16,
          "en": "and then the value as a string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 147.903,
          "en": "so red in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.46,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "And with that, this would be applied as a inline style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 155.67000000000002,
          "en": "right here in the JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.67000000000002,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "And if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 160.383,
          "en": "you indeed see that now the paragraph is red again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "And of course, this does not just work for colors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 169.35,
          "en": "but you can set any CSS styles like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.35,
          "end": 171.96,
          "en": "For example, also the text alignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.96,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "For that you just have to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 179.03,
          "en": "that text-align would be an invalid property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 180.453,
          "en": "in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 183.69,
          "en": "and therefore you either have to wrap this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.69,
          "end": 188.4,
          "en": "with single quotes, or more common and recommended,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 191.55,
          "en": "you have to switch to the camel case notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.55,
          "end": 193.14,
          "en": "where you omit the dash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.14,
          "end": 195.84,
          "en": "and you start the next word in the word",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.84,
          "end": 197.613,
          "en": "with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.78,
          "end": 201.723,
          "en": "And then you can set this to left, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 204.15,
          "en": "And with that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.15,
          "end": 206.49,
          "en": "it's actually still centered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.49,
          "end": 209.01,
          "en": "because it turns out that this styling here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.01,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "is actually not required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 214.02,
          "en": "though you can see that it is applied at least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.02,
          "end": 217.29,
          "en": "you also see that down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.29,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "In this app it just doesn't have an effect here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 221.34,
          "en": "for this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.34,
          "end": 224.04,
          "en": "because the header uses Flexbox,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.04,
          "end": 227.46,
          "en": "and automatically centers all its children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.46,
          "end": 229.29,
          "en": "If you disable that, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.29,
          "end": 231.873,
          "en": "you see indeed that it is on the left now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.97,
          "end": 237.54,
          "en": "But here I'll just reload and go back to the old styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.54,
          "end": 240.93,
          "en": "but this is how you could apply inline styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.93,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "and one advantage of this inline styling approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 248.61,
          "en": "is of course that these styles here really only affect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.61,
          "end": 251.52,
          "en": "the JSX element on which you add them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.52,
          "end": 256.35,
          "en": "And therefore using inline styles also has some advantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.35,
          "end": 258.42,
          "en": "and disadvantages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.42,
          "end": 262.14,
          "en": "And one advantage is that it's pretty easy to add them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.14,
          "end": 266.67,
          "en": "as you saw, and that the styles you do add as inline styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.67,
          "end": 269.88,
          "en": "only affect the element to which you add them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.88,
          "end": 271.803,
          "en": "and no other element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 275.88,
          "en": "Of course, this also has a disadvantage, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.88,
          "end": 280.29,
          "en": "because besides, of course, also having to know CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.29,
          "end": 281.85,
          "en": "when using inline styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.85,
          "end": 285.27,
          "en": "another disadvantage is that you have to style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 285.27,
          "end": 288.78,
          "en": "and target every element individually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.78,
          "end": 291.45,
          "en": "If you use style files here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.45,
          "end": 295.59000000000003,
          "en": "you can target all paragraphs with one rule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.59000000000003,
          "end": 297.48,
          "en": "and you don't have to add this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.48,
          "end": 299.82,
          "en": "to every paragraph on its own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 302.37,
          "en": "which is the case with inline styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.37,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "If we had multiple paragraphs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "that should all have this style here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 309.87,
          "en": "you would have to copy and paste this style prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.87,
          "end": 312.93,
          "en": "with its object here to all the paragraphs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.93,
          "end": 315.21,
          "en": "that should get this style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.21,
          "end": 317.01,
          "en": "And if you then wanna change the styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.01,
          "end": 320.073,
          "en": "you again have to do that for all paragraphs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.97,
          "end": 323.85,
          "en": "So that's definitely a disadvantage here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.85,
          "end": 328.14,
          "en": "And another potential disadvantage of using inline styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 328.14,
          "end": 332.58299999999997,
          "en": "is that you got no separation between CSS and JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.65999999999997,
          "end": 338.52,
          "en": "Instead, all your CSS code lives in your JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.52,
          "end": 342.12,
          "en": "which means the person who writes the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 342.12,
          "end": 346.5,
          "en": "probably also needs to be the person who adds the styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 346.5,
          "end": 350.22,
          "en": "or you and your designer constantly need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 350.22,
          "end": 353.43,
          "en": "to switch working on that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 353.43,
          "end": 357.18,
          "en": "since you both need to work on the JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 357.18,
          "end": 359.4,
          "en": "You for the structure and the logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 359.4,
          "end": 361.74,
          "en": "and your colleague for adding the styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 361.74,
          "end": 363.49,
          "en": "and that of course can be annoying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 364.53,
          "end": 368.4,
          "en": "But inline styles also have one more advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.4,
          "end": 369.42,
          "en": "I wanna mention,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 369.42,
          "end": 372.63,
          "en": "which we'll take a closer look at in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.63,
          "end": 375.15,
          "en": "Because with inline styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 375.15,
          "end": 377.91,
          "en": "adding and setting styles dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 377.91,
          "end": 380.28,
          "en": "conditionally to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.28,
          "end": 382.89300000000003,
          "en": "is pretty simple as you will see.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}